    "RowTrail receives the published minimal bootstrap and optional standard-library schema/finish/observe helpers. DuckDB receives concise persistent-connection instructions. Documentation lengths are not matched.",
    "Compared with alpha.5, both the bootstrap and profiling harness changed. The same requested model/settings and tasks do not make this a controlled model-latency A/B.",
    "DuckDB coverage ALL and one-row lookahead finalize scalar profiles without whole-result collection. Missing profiles remain unknown. Scan rows exclude metadata-only reads; physical source bytes are not measured for DuckDB.",
    "Source SQL statement counts exclude DESCRIBE/EXPLAIN and are logical statements, not physical scans. RowTrail source-reading job counts use recorded physical-byte metrics.",
    "Handoff setup materializes the subset before the agent starts. Setup time is reported separately and included in total; setup scans are excluded from agent I/O counters.",
    "Bridge response bytes include any on-demand schemas printed through rt.schema; separate USAGE.md file reads and CLI scaffolding are excluded. This byte metric is not total context/token usage, and differs from alpha.5 static schema-file reads.",
    "All 12 planned trials, including unsuccessful tool attempts, are retained without selective trial retries. This does not test progressive early stopping, real customer data or long-running multi-agent workloads."
